      "content": "I hear your inner turmoil, and it's completely understandable to feel this way. Feeling as if you're merely postponing an inevitable outcome can indeed be overwhelming. However, clinging to the belief that fighting the disease is pointless could potentially overlook possible advancements in medical science, alternative treatments, or even the chance to live your life to the fullest, making meaningful memories and contributions, regardless of the timeline. While pre-determined outcomes can be part of our lives, this in no way diminishes the value and impact the time you have. Every individual experience matters, and your feelings and choices contribute to your unique narrative. Each small step forward can provide a sense of purpose and control in ways that might be unexpected. If there's anything specific you would like to explore further, please let me know.",
      "source": "target",
